# Output of scripts/audit.sh.
#
# audit.sh writes to "${SCRIPT_DIR:-.}/security-audit-<host>-<ts>.log", so these land
# next to the script (or in the cwd) and show up as untracked files in `git status` --
# which is exactly how one gets committed by reflex.
#
# They are a full security posture dump of a live host: every listening socket, the
# sudoers file including NOPASSWD grants, authorized_keys owners, SSH login sources and
# brute-force origins, container env var NAMES, and unencrypted-private-key locations.
# That is a map of how to attack the box. This repo is public. Never commit one.
#
# No leading slash, so this matches at any depth.
security-audit-*.log
